          "text": "The DMA controller and the CPU both need the memory bus, and only one can use it at a time. The DMA controller takes the bus for the odd cycle here and there, which slightly slows the CPU down — this is called <strong>cycle stealing</strong>. It is a very small price, because it replaces the CPU copying every single byte by hand."
