        {
          "title": "FCFS and SSTF",
          "text": "<strong>FCFS</strong> is perfectly fair — no request is ever overtaken — but it makes no attempt to reduce movement, so the head can swing from cylinder 183 down to 37 and back up to 122. <strong>SSTF</strong> (Shortest Seek Time First) picks the request closest to the current head position, which is a great improvement, but it is essentially the SJF of disk scheduling and inherits the same flaw: a request at cylinder 190 can be starved indefinitely while new requests keep arriving near cylinder 50."
