      "realLife": "A lift in a ten-storey building. FCFS is a lift that goes to floors in exactly the order the buttons were pressed — up to 8, down to 2, up to 7. SSTF goes to the nearest requested floor, which may leave the person on floor 10 waiting all day. SCAN is a normal lift: it sweeps all the way up, then all the way down. LOOK is a smarter lift that turns around at the highest floor anyone actually asked for, instead of pointlessly going to the tenth.",
      "worked": "<strong>The standard worked example.</strong> Request queue (cylinders): <strong>98, 183, 37, 122, 14, 124, 65, 67</strong>. The head starts at cylinder <strong>53</strong>. The disk has cylinders <strong>0 to 199</strong>. For SCAN, C-SCAN, LOOK and C-LOOK we assume the head is moving <strong>towards the higher cylinder numbers</strong>.<br><br>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━<br><strong>1. FCFS</strong> — serve in the given order.<br>Order: 53 → 98 → 183 → 37 → 122 → 14 → 124 → 65 → 67<br>Movements: |98-53| = 45, |183-98| = 85, |37-183| = 146, |122-37| = 85, |14-122| = 108, |124-14| = 110, |65-124| = 59, |67-65| = 2<br>45 + 85 + 146 + 85 + 108 + 110 + 59 + 2<br><strong>Total head movement = 640 cylinders.</strong><br><br>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━<br><strong>2. SSTF</strong> — always go to the nearest pending request.<br>From 53: nearest is 65 (distance 12). → 65<br>From 65: nearest is 67 (2). → 67<br>From 67: 37 is 30 away, 98 is 31 away → 37 wins. → 37<br>From 37: nearest is 14 (23). → 14<br>From 14: only higher ones left; nearest is 98 (84). → 98<br>From 98: nearest is 122 (24). → 122<br>From 122: nearest is 124 (2). → 124<br>From 124: last one is 183 (59). → 183<br>Order: 53 → 65 → 67 → 37 → 14 → 98 → 122 → 124 → 183<br>12 + 2 + 30 + 23 + 84 + 24 + 2 + 59<br><strong>Total head movement = 236 cylinders.</strong><br><br>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━<br><strong>3. SCAN</strong> — go up to the end (199), then reverse.<br>Order: 53 → 65 → 67 → 98 → 122 → 124 → 183 → <strong>199</strong> → 37 → 14<br>Up: 199 - 53 = 146<br>Down: 199 - 14 = 185<br>146 + 185<br><strong>Total head movement = 331 cylinders.</strong><br><br>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━<br><strong>4. C-SCAN</strong> — go up to 199, jump to 0, continue upward.<br>Order: 53 → 65 → 67 → 98 → 122 → 124 → 183 → <strong>199</strong> → <strong>0</strong> → 14 → 37<br>Up: 199 - 53 = 146<br>Jump back: 199 - 0 = 199<br>Up again: 37 - 0 = 37<br>146 + 199 + 37<br><strong>Total head movement = 382 cylinders.</strong><br><br>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━<br><strong>5. LOOK</strong> — like SCAN, but turn back at the last request (183), not at 199.<br>Order: 53 → 65 → 67 → 98 → 122 → <strong>124 → 183</strong> → 37 → 14<br>Up: 183 - 53 = 130<br>Down: 183 - 14 = 169<br>130 + 169<br><strong>Total head movement = 299 cylinders.</strong><br><br>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━<br><strong>6. C-LOOK</strong> — like C-SCAN, but jump back to the lowest request (14), not to 0.<br>Order: 53 → 65 → 67 → 98 → 122 → 124 → <strong>183</strong> → <strong>14</strong> → 37<br>Up: 183 - 53 = 130<br>Jump back: 183 - 14 = 169<br>Up again: 37 - 14 = 23<br>130 + 169 + 23<br><strong>Total head movement = 322 cylinders.</strong><br><br>━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━<br><strong>Final comparison (head at 53, moving upward):</strong><br>FCFS = 640 · SSTF = <strong>236 (best here)</strong> · SCAN = 331 · C-SCAN = 382 · LOOK = 299 · C-LOOK = 322<br><br>Two things to notice. First, <strong>LOOK always beats SCAN</strong> and <strong>C-LOOK always beats C-SCAN</strong>, because they never travel to an end of the disk with no requests on it. Second, SSTF wins on total distance here, but it is the only one of the six that can <strong>starve</strong> a request — so the lowest number is not automatically the best algorithm. Always add that sentence in the exam.",
